    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a high-upside slate today, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (78.03) and **Kyle Tucker** (76.41), who command the top spots in our daily efficiency rankings. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an elite combination of a hitter-friendly park and a favorable matchup against Schultz, whose 5.16 xERA suggests he will struggle to contain our middle-infield anchor. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** finds himself in a prime position against J.T. Ginn; his ability to capitalize on favorable park factors and the positive platoon split makes him a cornerstone for today\u2019s production. **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) and **Andy Pages** (70.62) round out a potent offensive core, with **Jackson Merrill** specifically benefiting from a wind-out scenario that elevates his raw power potential against Colin Rea.\n\nStrategic optimization favored high-ceiling matchups over players battling difficult arms or poor platoon splits. **Sam Antonacci** (55.23) remains in the lineup despite the tough matchup against Dean Kremer (2.22 xERA) because his elite park factors and top-of-the-order designation mitigate the risk. Our most difficult decision involved keeping **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** on the bench; while he possesses a respectable 49.05 score, he fell just short of the threshold, largely due to a prohibitive dynamic platoon penalty against the left-handed Payton Tolle and a lingering 30% rain risk. We are also monitoring **Nasim Nunez** closely; despite his utility, the rain risk and a difficult order slot make his 51.77 score a fragile start, requiring us to remain vigilant as official lineups materialize.",
